{"task": "IG-2B05", "path": "docs/IG-WGU-ARCHITECTURE.md", "start_line": 1, "lines": ["# WGC architecture", "", "This is the active architectural proposal; machine contracts are established task by", "task. [Queue](work/queue.json) defines execution order, [data model](IG-DATA-MODEL.md)", "defines record invariants, and [runtime contract](IG-LEGAL-ACTIONS.md) defines gameplay.", "", "```mermaid", "flowchart LR", "  KB[WGU KB] --> IN[Frozen inputs and read-only adapter]", "  SRC[Complete rulebook and required materials] --> INV[Independent source inventory]", "  IN --> IG[Source IG with evidence and gaps]", "  INV --> IG", "  IG --> SEM[Typed rule semantics]", "  SEM --> REV[Source review and human acceptance]", "  REV --> REF[Reference executor]", "  REV --> COMP[Compiler]", "  COMP --> PKG[Immutable rules package]", "  PKG --> RUN[Deterministic legal runtime]", "  REF --> EQ[Differential checks]", "  RUN --> EQ", "  RUN --> VIEW[Player view and exact choices]", "  VIEW --> AI[Strategy selection]", "  AI --> VAL[Validate against current revision]", "  VAL --> RUN", "```", "", "## Ownership and boundaries", "", "WGU maintains its KB. WGC reads a frozen directory snapshot and original documents,", "preserves both, records discrepancies, and builds versioned interpretations.", "It never edits WGU as an import side effect. Corrections are separate WGC proposals.", "The runtime owns authoritative game state and history; an LLM description is not state.", "AI owns strategy only. UI, online services, providers, and a graph database are not", "prerequisites. Start with local JSON/JSONL, deterministic exports and derived indexes.", "", "| Module / future path | Responsibility | Output |", "|---|---|---|", "| `src/wgc/inputs/` | Snapshot, safe paths, hashes, availability | Immutable input manifest |", "| `src/wgc/wgu_adapter/` | Safe parsing, unknown fields, identities | Import records and origin bindings |", "| `src/wgc/sources/` | Pages, regions, evidence, independent inventory | Coverage denominator |", "| `src/wgc/reconcile/` | Matches, disagreements, omissions, editions | Source IG and explicit gaps |", "| `src/wgc/review/` | Review packets, decisions, freshness | Revision-scoped decision ledger |", "| `src/wgc/semantics/` | Types, expressions, actions, procedure IR | Formal IG linked to source clauses |", "| `src/wgc/reference/` | Simple deterministic execution | Independent comparison baseline |", "| `src/wgc/compiler/` | Type/closure checks and lowering | Reproducible executable package |", "| `src/wgc/runtime/` | Actions, validation, events, replay | State transitions and legal choices |", "| `src/wgc/player/` | Visibility, compact views and deltas | Player-safe decision interface |", "", "These are planned boundaries, not existing implementations. Tests live in corresponding", "`tests/<module>/` directories; public fixtures are synthetic. Source-derived data lives", "in `private/ig/projects/spqr/`. Planning tools in `scripts/` do not implement these modules.", "", "## Existing input evidence", "", "The 2026-10-11 textual inspection recorded 523 rules (438 core, 85 scenario-book),", "233 relations, 48 tables, 134 terms, 79 ambiguities, 3 changes, 59 control questions,", "11 main procedures, 4 subprocedures and 80 steps. These are inventory observations,", "not successful YAML/schema validation or source review. The 27 inspected files were", "hashed. All 36 configured source paths were unavailable at that inspection.", "The private inventory is preserved under `private/ig/planning/wgu-spqr-2026-10-11/`.", "Recheck bytes when implementing; do not turn these counts into hard-coded gold.", "", "An archived 44-page SPQR 5E PDF has been copied, hash-verified, into the active source", "registry `private/ig/sources/spqr-5e/`. Its provenance records the old path and hash.", "Identity with WGU's unavailable original is **unknown**. Explicitly pin it as the source", "of a new IG; reconcile WGU content against it rather than claiming to recover WGU's original.", "", "## Import contract", "", "Primary input: game `wgu.yaml`, complete `kb/`, and explicitly enumerated auxiliary", "files. The optional `wgu/kb-bundle@1` route is later work: the current exporter omits", "some auxiliary files and full source configuration, abbreviates revision information,", "and adds a generation time. A bundle alone cannot establish complete input accounting.", "", "Freeze raw bytes, relative paths, sizes, SHA-256, schema/adapter versions and import", "configuration. Git commit and dirty state are supporting metadata; record unknown", "when inaccessible. Detect source changes during snapshotting. Reject unsafe YAML tags,", "duplicate keys, traversal, and paths escaping the allowlist; preserve unknown fields.", "Unavailable PDFs block source verification, not import of available KB records.", ""], "truncated": true}

